Description:

BMPS.COM converts MSX's BSAVE format graphic file to BMP format, 
often used as Windows' desktop patern and so no. BMPS.COM can 
handle following formats of graphic file:

    .SC5     SCREEN 5 BSAVE FILE (256*212,with pallet)
    .SC7     SCREEN 7 BSAVE FILE (512*212,with pallet)
    .SC8     SCREEN 8 BSAVE FILE (256*212,no pallet)
    .SCA/SCB SCREEN 10/11 BSAVE FILE (256*212,with pallet)
    .SCC     SCREEN 12 BSAVE FILE (256*212,no pallet)
    .SC0+SC1 SCREEN 7 INTERLACED BSAVE FILE (512*424,with pallet)

BMPS.COM would load pallet table in .SC? or by .PL?.


System Requirements:

BMPS.COM requires MSX-DOS(1) or later. And Displaying the graphic 
files, ofcorse MSX must be able to use the display mode.


Usage:

A>BMPS [loadfile [writedrive:]] [/X]

     loadfile - BSAVE filename, or wild-cards, to convert.
  writedrive: - Drive name to put BMP file created.
           /X - Auto convertion without any key inputs.


conveted BMP file's format:

         Source mode  Pixels   Colors     Filesize
            SCREEN 5  256*212  pallet*16    27,254
            SCREEN 7  512*424  pallet*16   108,662
            SCREEN 8  256*212  pallet*256   55,350
        SCREEN 10/11  256*212  16million   162,870
           SCREEN 12  256*212  16million   162,870
 SCREEN 7 Interlaced  512*424  pallet*16   108,662


